      ":question/problem": "What is the exact value of $\\sin\\left(-\\frac{17\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator?\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-\\frac{17\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{5\\pi}{3}$.*",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $-\\frac{17\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{5\\pi}{3}$.\n\nRecall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y)=\\sin x\\cos y-\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(-\\frac{17\\pi}{12}\\right) &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)-\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
