      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $\\frac{17\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$.\n\nRecall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x+y)=\\sin x\\cos y+\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(\\frac{17\\pi}{12}\\right) &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right)+\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{-\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
