      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $-\\frac{13\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{4\\pi}{3}$.\n\nRecall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y)=\\sin x\\cos y-\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(-\\frac{13\\pi}{12}\\right) &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\right)-\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
